# Conventional Commits

Commit messages and pull request titles must be [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) so git-cliff can update `CHANGELOG.md`.

```text
type(scope): short description
```

Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`.

```text
# ❌ BAD
Add changelog automation
Updated the init script

# ✅ GOOD
feat(init): add --from export flag for existing mbtiles
fix(overture): raise open-file limit before invoking tippecanoe
docs: add MkDocs documentation site
chore(ci): add git-cliff changelog workflow
```

Breaking changes: `feat!: ...` or a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer. Do not hand-edit `CHANGELOG.md` for ordinary work; the Changelog workflow regenerates it. Changelog bot commits use `chore(changelog): update CHANGELOG.md [skip ci]`.
